(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[16 1 "// The module _hashlib (queue 537): Modules/_hashopenssl.c of CPython 3.14.10 over Go's crypto in place of OpenSSL's EVP"] [17 1 "// interface, as _ssl is over Go's crypto/tls (PYS22 (a)): hashlib.py and hmac.py take it first when it imports. Its"] [18 1 "// names: new(name, data=b'', *, usedforsecurity=True, string=None) and openssl_md5 ... openssl_shake_256 (the types"] [19 1 "// HASH and HASHXOF, a subclass of HASH: update, digest, hexdigest, copy; name, digest_size, block_size; repr"] [20 1 "// \"<NAME _hashlib.HASH object @ ADDRESS>\"; DISALLOW_INSTANTIATION), hmac_new(key, msg=b'', digestmod=None) (the type"] [21 1 "// HMAC, builtins_hmac.go's hmacObject with this module's type), hmac_digest(key, msg, digest), pbkdf2_hmac,"] [22 1 "// scrypt, compare_digest, get_fips_mode (0: no FIPS provider), openssl_md_meth_names, _constructors (a mappingproxy of"] [23 1 "// the openssl_* functions to their names), UnsupportedDigestmodError (a ValueError) and _GIL_MINSIZE. The digests are"] [24 1 "// the ones py_hashes names that Go's crypto has (md5, sha1, sha2 with the truncated sha512s, sha3, shake and blake2,"] [25 1 "// the last by hashlib_blake2.go); a name is found as py_digest_by_name finds it: the Python name, else OpenSSL's"] [26 1 "// names and aliases, which OpenSSL's fetch takes in any case. OpenSSL's further digests (md5-sha1, ripemd160, sm3)"] [27 1 "// are not offered: they are absent from openssl_md_meth_names, and new() refuses them as an unsupported digest. The"] [28 1 "// errors that OpenSSL's error queue words are given in its words: \"[digital envelope routines] unsupported\" for an"] [29 1 "// unknown digest, \"no reason supplied\" for an HMAC over an XOF, scrypt's \"memory limit exceeded\"."] [31 1 "// osslMD is a py_hashentry_t with what Go needs to make the digest."] [33 31 "// py_digest_name's"] [35 41 "// nil: a shake or blake2"] [37 29 "// blake2b"] [79 1 "// osslByName is the module's hashtable (the Python names) and osslByAlias OpenSSL's names and aliases (lower case:"] [80 1 "// EVP_MD_fetch compares them without case)."] [118 1 "// osslUnsupported is the module's UnsupportedDigestmodError, made once (a module per interpreter shares it, as"] [119 1 "// builtins_hmac.go's UnknownHashError)."] [134 1 "// osslDigestByName is py_digest_by_name."] [145 1 "// osslConstructors is the module state's constructs: each openssl_* function and its digest's name, made once with the"] [146 1 "// functions (osslConstructorNames' order) by the first module made."] [154 1 "// osslDigestByDigestmod is py_digest_by_digestmod: a str by name, else one of the openssl_* functions."] [164 45 "// PyDict_GetItemWithError's"] [175 1 "// osslHMAC is hmac_new's HMAC_Init_ex: an XOF is refused by OpenSSL with no reason on its queue."] [185 1 "// osslBuffer is a Py_buffer argument of Argument Clinic: any bytes-like object (a str refused)."] [193 1 "// osslLong is clinic's long converter."] [211 1 "// pbkdf2HMAC is PKCS5_PBKDF2_HMAC (RFC 8018 §5.2) over the HMAC of hmacNew."] [247 1 "// salsa208 is the Salsa20/8 core (RFC 7914 §3) on b, in place."] [289 1 "// scryptBlockMix is scryptBlockMix (RFC 7914 §4) of b (2r blocks of 16 words) into y."] [298 3 "// even blocks first, then odd ones"] [304 1 "// scryptROMix is scryptROMix (RFC 7914 §5) on b, 128*r bytes, in place."] [333 1 "// osslScryptCheck is EVP_PBE_scrypt's parameter checks (crypto/evp/pbe_scrypt.c, OpenSSL 3's kdf_scrypt.c): 0 ok,"] [334 1 "// 1 an invalid combination (no reason queued), 2 a check that queues EVP_R_MEMORY_LIMIT_EXCEEDED (p*r, N against 2^(16r),"] [335 1 "// the memory limit: SCRYPT_MAX_MEM, 32 MiB, when maxmem is 0)."] [422 23 "// EVP_DigestFinal of an XOF fails with no reason queued"] [554 4 "// _hashlib.new(name, data=b'', *, usedforsecurity=True, string=None)"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[136 26] [139 44] [156 30] [159 34] [160 37] [164 30] [187 24] [195 24] [216 24] [216 49] [229 20] [229 